    "narrative": "With **Josh Naylor** (65.60) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (60.99) anchoring the lineup, we are well-positioned for offensive output against what are, at best, league-average arms. **Josh Naylor** is our top play today, benefiting from a favorable platoon split against Chandler and a prime cleanup spot that boosts his RBI floor. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a solid matchup against Roupp; his score is buoyed by a strong platoon advantage and a projected spot in the four-hole. While **Jose Caballero** (56.02) sits just outside the 60+ \"Strong\" tier, he is a fascinating play; he faces a tough pitcher in Early, but his ability to exploit a slow delivery makes him a unique source of SB production, which remains our primary objective in this 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision was bypassing **Henry Bolte** (49.78) for the remaining utility slots, as his leadoff status provides significant R and SB upside. However, the current optimizer favors the more stable profiles of **Josh Naylor** and **Tyler Soderstrom** to avoid unnecessary cap burn on lower-efficiency outcomes. We are monitoring **James Wood** (48.39) closely; while his 0.401 xwOBA suggests an elite talent, the matchup against S\u00e1nchez is a distinct \"SP Skill\" disadvantage that necessitates caution. We are relieved that **Corbin Carroll** is out of the lineup due to a rainout, sparing us the choice between his high-ceiling potential and our currently healthy starters. \n\nBe advised that volatility remains high with several pieces of our core. **James Wood** bears the highest risk today due to his poor BvP history and a tough lefty-on-lefty matchup. While we are running with **Max Muncy** (45.36) and **Cole Young** (44.97) to fill out the middle infield, keep a close eye on the late-breaking lineups for any changes to the order, as these marginal plays are highly sensitive to batting position. Our bench remains depleted, with **Vinnie Pasquantino** on the IL and both **Mickey Moniak** and **Austin Riley** sitting on a scheduled off-day, meaning we must rely on the consistency of the current starters to preserve our remaining game caps for the weekend push.",
